 ## Background
-Panoptic Lifting was introduced in 2023 by the authors of "Panoptic Lifting for 3D Scene Understanding with Neural Fields" [S1]. It addresses the limitations of prior panoptic NeRF methods (like Panoptic NeRF and DM-NeRF) which required manual ground truth or coarse meshes, by lifting machine-generated 2D panoptic labels into a consistent 3D representation [S1]. It builds on [TensoRF](13550-model-architecture-and-encoding.md) for efficient density and color representation [S1].
+Panoptic Lifting was introduced in "Panoptic Lifting for 3D Scene Understanding with Neural Fields" (CVPR 2023) [S1]. It addresses the challenge of learning panoptic 3D volumetric representations from in-the-wild scenes without manual 3D ground truth, relying instead on machine-generated 2D panoptic segmentation masks [S1]. It builds on [Model Architecture and Encoding](13550-model-architecture-and-encoding.md) and [TensoRF](4) for the base radiance field representation [S1].
 
